1
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:35,030
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:37,710
[Episode 32]

3
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,220
Yizhong.

4
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:04,320
Well,

5
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,600
find some time

6
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,220
to bring Yingjie over for dinner.

7
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:10,420
She's been too busy with work recently.

8
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,780
She can't be that busy.

9
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:14,630
You should at least do right by her,

10
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:15,030
right?

11
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,050
How about

12
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,630
you get married this year?

13
00:03:19,050 --> 00:03:20,180
Look how old you are.

14
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,570
Hurry up and have a baby.

15
00:03:23,190 --> 00:03:24,050
Mom, say something to him.

16
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:25,450
What is he talking about?

17
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:26,310
Chen Fan,

18
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:27,970
shut up.

19
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:38,920
Hello.

20
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:41,630
Yes.

21
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:47,000
What?

22
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:56,800
Wait, I...

23
00:03:58,079 --> 00:03:59,680
I mean... Where is she now?

24
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:53,400
This is the place where Yingjie lived.

25
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,940
All her things are inside.

26
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:30,390
Yingjie's matter

27
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:33,920
has caused trouble for the organization.

28
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:34,520
Not at all.

29
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,040
I heard her performance...

30
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,170
It was outstanding.

31
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,460
Yingjie was outstanding.

32
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:05,830
Perhaps

33
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:10,260
it was her name
that brought her misfortune.

34
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,000
Ma'am.

35
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,530
What's wrong with you two?

36
00:07:34,450 --> 00:07:36,510
Do you want to be photographed again?

37
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:38,830
What did you do?

38
00:07:38,890 --> 00:07:39,830
What did you do to Xia Yingjie?

39
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:40,290
Enough.

40
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,000
What did you do?

41
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:41,750
That's enough!

42
00:07:41,750 --> 00:07:42,390
There's a trial this afternoon!

43
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:43,070
What are you doing, Chen Yizhong?

44
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:44,360
She died right after arguing with you.

45
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,000
What happened?

46
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:45,720
What happened?

47
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,800
Yes, just like you said.

48
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,630
It's exactly what the rumors say.

49
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:48,650
After I argued with her,

50
00:07:48,650 --> 00:07:50,360
she got hit by a car and died.
Are you satisfied?

51
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:50,760
You...

52
00:07:51,770 --> 00:07:53,000
-I'm satisfied?
-Alright, that's enough.

53
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:53,630
Are you satisfied?

54
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:54,090
Enough!

55
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,260
Enough.

56
00:08:00,090 --> 00:08:01,120
If I go to the hospital

57
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:01,580
and get a check-up now,

58
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:03,630
it's got to be at least minor injuries,
right?

59
00:08:03,630 --> 00:08:05,600
You're the principal offender,
and you're the accomplice.

60
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,310
Both of you will get locked up.

61
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:07,040
Hu Xudong can just

62
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,050
rot in prison waiting to die!

63
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:09,250
Don't act like a jerk.

64
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,870
I'm just asking you one thing.

65
00:08:10,870 --> 00:08:13,120
What exactly happened to Xia Yingjie?

66
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:16,720
Yu Gaoyuan, stop pretending!

67
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,650
I know you're feeling guilty too!

68
00:08:17,650 --> 00:08:18,550
Just tell us plainly!

69
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:20,410
She was targeted in retaliation!

70
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:25,330
A wife‑abuser she tried

71
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,280
got released!

72
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:26,870
He'd been

73
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:27,950
staking out the courthouse gate for days!

74
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:28,480
When she wasn't paying attention,

75
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,480
he pushed her onto the road,
and she was hit and killed!

76
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:34,299
The driver was drunk and unlicensed!

77
00:08:36,270 --> 00:08:37,669
What about the murderer?

78
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,320
He's been arrested.

79
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,179
The driver has been arrested too.

80
00:08:46,670 --> 00:08:48,670
She passed away without suffering.

81
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,260
Let me say a couple of things
that are out of line.

82
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,200
For Hu Xudong's sake,

83
00:09:10,030 --> 00:09:11,670
just ask him to plead guilty,
offer compensation,

84
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,150
and stop being so stubborn.

85
00:09:13,150 --> 00:09:15,080
Try to get him a suspended death sentence.

86
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,270
I'll try to delay the sentencing
as long as I can,

87
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:18,200
but I can't hold it off for too long.

88
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,200
Now your conscience kicks in?

89
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,000
Isn't it a lawyer's job to make sure

90
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,930
someone who shouldn't die

91
00:09:27,930 --> 00:09:29,730
gets to live as long as possible?

92
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:38,840
See you in court.

93
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,370
Hello, this is Zhang Lihui.

94
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,000
Yu.

95
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,840
How did you get my number?

96
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,010
I'm

97
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:58,870
quite annoying, right?

98
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:08,250
Do you have to go in person?

99
00:12:09,570 --> 00:12:11,100
Can't you just have someone

100
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,480
ask around for you?

101
00:12:13,910 --> 00:12:15,120
I have to go in person.

102
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:21,160
If I had known you were so stubborn,

103
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:25,240
I wouldn't have gotten together with you.

104
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,840
I'm an old liar.

105
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,360
Alright, alright.

106
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,390
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

107
00:12:35,390 --> 00:12:36,200
I'm sorry.

108
00:12:36,550 --> 00:12:37,000
Right?

109
00:12:37,630 --> 00:12:38,690
Alright, alright.

110
00:12:50,010 --> 00:12:51,390
[Procuratorate Office‌ in Bieshan Prison]

111
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:54,210
Mr. Guo.

112
00:12:55,510 --> 00:12:56,240
You're here.

113
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:01,510
Prosecutor Guo, you're finally here.

114
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:02,110
Yan Jicai!

115
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:04,630
Keep your emotions in check.

116
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:07,440
Can you answer

117
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:08,550
my questions?

118
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:09,440
Yes.

119
00:13:12,270 --> 00:13:14,010
Get him some paper

120
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:14,890
and a pen.

121
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,410
Sit closer to me.

122
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:17,750
Go.

123
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:21,120
You've lost weight.

124
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,570
You've lost weight.

125
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,370
He said you've lost weight.

126
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:29,540
I've lost a little weight,

127
00:13:29,790 --> 00:13:31,790
but that won't kill me anytime soon.

128
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:46,350
Maybe we should call it a day.

129
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:47,210
I'm tired.

130
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:53,310
By the way,

131
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,950
can you improve my meals?

132
00:13:58,910 --> 00:13:59,850
I love meat.

133
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,660
Prosecutor Zhang,

134
00:14:03,670 --> 00:14:04,870
what Jia Peng confessed today

135
00:14:04,870 --> 00:14:05,340
is very important.

136
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,600
We need to head back to the bureau
to report right away.

137
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,320
I'll go back with you.

138
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:07,650
Okay.

139
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:11,120
Jia Peng said

140
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,240
Lin Yan was wearing

141
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,080
pale blue briefs

142
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,610
with little red polka dots.

143
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:15,910
Did he confess this himself,

144
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:16,530
or did you guide

145
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:17,390
and prompt him?

146
00:14:18,510 --> 00:14:19,240
Captain Zhang.

147
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,700
He blurted it out himself.

148
00:14:20,870 --> 00:14:21,910
Did he say

149
00:14:22,390 --> 00:14:23,360
where the briefs

150
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:24,440
ended up?

151
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,700
They were stuffed entirely
inside Lin Yan's mouth.

152
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:29,890
Alright.

153
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:31,270
You guys go out first.

154
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,250
I remember Yan Jicai

155
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:40,120
never mentioned this detail back then.

156
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:40,550
It was us back then...

157
00:14:40,550 --> 00:14:41,610
Alright, alright.

158
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:42,960
I know.

159
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,510
Has the DNA sample been sent for testing?

160
00:14:47,510 --> 00:14:49,770
Yes, to the Ministry of Public Security.

161
00:14:51,270 --> 00:14:52,790
If there is a match,

162
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:56,630
Yan Jicai's conviction will collapse.

163
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:07,240
What?

164
00:15:12,630 --> 00:15:13,760
You got it out of him?

165
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,000
It was really him?

166
00:15:33,790 --> 00:15:34,520
Captain Lyu.

167
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:36,410
Please help me recall

168
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:39,550
if Yan Jicai ever volunteered
those details

169
00:15:39,550 --> 00:15:40,760
back then

170
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,170
about the briefs that Jia Peng mentioned.

171
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:44,480
What do you mean?

172
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,390
Are you saying

173
00:15:46,390 --> 00:15:47,750
we induced him into confessing back then?

174
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:48,730
How could anyone

175
00:15:49,270 --> 00:15:50,510
describe it so precisely

176
00:15:50,510 --> 00:15:52,510
unless he was the real perpetrator?

177
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,080
A pair of pale blue briefs

178
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,210
with red polka dots.

179
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:57,360
Only a very small number of people

180
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,120
could possbily know

181
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,180
such information.

182
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:01,430
Isn't that enough, Captain Lyu?

183
00:16:03,190 --> 00:16:04,390
Based on this single confession,

184
00:16:04,390 --> 00:16:05,650
anything is possible.

185
00:16:05,910 --> 00:16:07,640
Don't we also have the DNA test?

186
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,700
Now you trust the DNA test?

187
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,550
I've already made a mistake once.

188
00:16:14,550 --> 00:16:16,350
I don't want to make a second one.

189
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:19,180
I'm not saying
we arrested the wrong person.

190
00:16:20,550 --> 00:16:21,950
I checked the case files.

191
00:16:22,310 --> 00:16:24,010
It wasn't until his second-to-last

192
00:16:24,010 --> 00:16:25,120
confession that Yan Jicai

193
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,250
started mentioning

194
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:27,170
stuffing the briefs

195
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:28,370
into Lin Yan's mouth.

196
00:16:28,510 --> 00:16:28,980
But

197
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,480
he didn't provide a specific description

198
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,210
of what the briefs looked like.

199
00:16:32,430 --> 00:16:33,480
That confession

200
00:16:33,550 --> 00:16:34,870
was already very close

201
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:36,270
to his final guilty plea.

202
00:16:36,510 --> 00:16:38,170
You must have seen the actual item.

203
00:16:38,170 --> 00:16:39,830
There are photos in the files.

204
00:16:40,030 --> 00:16:41,240
I saw photocopies,

205
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:44,030
which were black and white
and also very blurry.

206
00:16:44,030 --> 00:16:45,080
Was it a pair

207
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:47,960
of pale blue briefs with red polka dots,

208
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:48,930
Captain Lyu?

209
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:51,120
Let's wait

210
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,520
for the DNA test results.

211
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:01,670
You already have your answer in your mind,

212
00:17:01,670 --> 00:17:02,270
don't you?

213
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:06,270
Captain Lyu!

214
00:17:06,270 --> 00:17:07,000
Captain Lyu!

215
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,380
Hurry! Call an ambulance!

216
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:10,520
Hurry, hurry!

217
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:11,460
How are you, sir?

218
00:17:15,790 --> 00:17:16,990
Family of Gao Qiuyue!

219
00:17:18,030 --> 00:17:18,920
Family of Gao Qiuyue!

220
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,119
Come with me quickly.

221
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:28,140
Mom.

222
00:17:29,510 --> 00:17:30,350
Mom!

223
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:32,400
Mom!

224
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:35,590
Mom!

225
00:17:38,590 --> 00:17:39,680
Mom!

226
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:02,240
Xiaowen.

227
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,510
Your mom is gone.

228
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:07,480
I'm

229
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:10,260
leaving too.

230
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:29,200
You need to take good care of yourself.

231
00:19:18,390 --> 00:19:19,760
Have you heard?

232
00:19:20,350 --> 00:19:22,110
Four stents all at once.

233
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,380
-It cost so much.
-Mentor.

234
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,680
How are you doing?

235
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:28,290
Here.

236
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:29,310
Sit down and talk.

237
00:19:29,310 --> 00:19:30,000
Let me handle this, Ma'am.

238
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:30,600
It's fine.

239
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:34,590
You're so busy,
and you still came to see me.

240
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:35,990
It's the least I could do.

241
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:36,930
I'm fine.

242
00:19:38,830 --> 00:19:40,030
Have the DNA test results

243
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:40,760
come out yet?

244
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:42,270
What DNA test?

245
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:43,510
Where did you get

246
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:44,310
a DNA test?

247
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:46,070
Don't you think this guy

248
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:47,730
needs a stent in his brain too?

249
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:50,160
Alright, alright.
I need to talk to Chief Jiang.

250
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,200
You head out first.

251
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,240
You're in this condition,

252
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,300
and you're still talking about work?

253
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,100
You head out first. Hurry.

254
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,600
Talk some sense into him.

255
00:20:02,890 --> 00:20:04,070
The doctor said your blood vessels

256
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:05,040
are all clogged up.

257
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,320
Just get some rest.

258
00:20:06,350 --> 00:20:07,680
Stop pushing yourself.

259
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,110
A joint investigation team

260
00:20:14,110 --> 00:20:15,830
of the police, procuratorate and court
has been set up.

261
00:20:15,830 --> 00:20:16,640
I'm in it too.

262
00:20:17,070 --> 00:20:17,800
Don't worry.

263
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,590
What's true can't be made false,

264
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:21,590
and what's false can't be made true.

265
00:20:27,490 --> 00:20:28,830
Aside from the white sandals

266
00:20:28,830 --> 00:20:29,720
and the briefs,

267
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,880
is there any other new

268
00:20:32,110 --> 00:20:33,110
valuable lead?

269
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,110
Don't worry too much.

270
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:38,540
Jia Peng isn't necessarily
the real killer.

271
00:20:40,070 --> 00:20:40,590
Look.

272
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,200
The details he confessed

273
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,400
are indeed accurate.

274
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:45,890
Outsiders couldn't have known them.

275
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:47,790
Yet there are major flaws overall.

276
00:20:47,790 --> 00:20:48,920
The timeline is off,

277
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,810
and the sequence of events doesn't add up.

278
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,560
That's very suspicious.

279
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:56,240
What if

280
00:20:57,120 --> 00:20:58,170
the DNA match

281
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:58,920
comes back positive?

282
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:00,640
We still can't take it as absolute truth.

283
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,830
This technology hasn't been around
for long.

284
00:21:02,830 --> 00:21:03,890
What if it's wrong?

285
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:04,840
Who knows?

286
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:07,830
My sister-in-law

287
00:21:07,830 --> 00:21:09,720
works at the Provincial Department's
Technical Division.

288
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:11,070
She says even with a match,

289
00:21:11,070 --> 00:21:12,550
there's still a one‑in‑a‑million chance

290
00:21:12,550 --> 00:21:13,480
that it's wrong.

291
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:18,280
Don't stare at me like that.

292
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:19,770
It makes me nervous.

293
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,340
You're comforting me, right?

294
00:21:28,270 --> 00:21:28,800
Alright.

295
00:21:29,270 --> 00:21:30,270
Get some good rest.

296
00:21:30,270 --> 00:21:31,160
I've got work to do.

297
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,560
I'll come back tomorrow.

298
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:33,510
Don't come again.

299
00:21:33,510 --> 00:21:34,800
I'll be discharged in a couple of days.

300
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:35,680
Get some good rest.

301
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:36,160
Okay.

302
00:21:56,550 --> 00:21:57,000
Dad.

303
00:21:57,690 --> 00:21:58,250
Dad.

304
00:22:01,510 --> 00:22:01,920
Look.

305
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:02,670
Siyi.

306
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:03,320
You...

307
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,350
Look.

308
00:22:07,550 --> 00:22:08,350
I can walk now.

309
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,180
Do you want some water?

310
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,260
I'll pour you some.

311
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:15,270
No, no.

312
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:16,200
I don't want any.

313
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:17,080
Come here.

314
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:22,820
What are you...

315
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:24,930
Dad.

316
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,590
Can I ask you a favor?

317
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,010
What is it?

318
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:32,270
Tell me.

319
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,490
I'll agree to anything.

320
00:22:36,340 --> 00:22:37,340
Can we never

321
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,760
mention that incident again?

322
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,940
You won't mention it. I won't mention it.

323
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,330
Nobody will mention it.

324
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:48,370
We won't mention it to anyone else.

325
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:49,480
Okay?

326
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,130
Put this over there.

327
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:04,610
Then let me ask you.

328
00:23:06,310 --> 00:23:08,790
Will you go back to the gymnastics team?

329
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:12,170
I want to start over

330
00:23:12,830 --> 00:23:14,490
and find something else to do.

331
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,130
The lady named Zhou Tong

332
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:16,880
told me

333
00:23:17,510 --> 00:23:19,110
that she could help me become a journalist

334
00:23:19,110 --> 00:23:19,880
or a lawyer.

335
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:23,000
She also told me

336
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:25,030
not to keep dwelling on this

337
00:23:26,790 --> 00:23:27,920
but to move forward.

338
00:23:31,110 --> 00:23:31,790
Dad, look.

339
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,400
I can stand up now.

340
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,680
Okay, don't move.

341
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:41,930
I promise you

342
00:23:43,590 --> 00:23:45,250
that I won't mention it again.

343
00:23:50,790 --> 00:23:51,240
Siyi.

344
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,240
You know what?

345
00:23:56,030 --> 00:23:57,090
In all these years,

346
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:58,550
this is the first time you've talked

347
00:23:58,550 --> 00:23:59,480
so much to me.

348
00:24:05,550 --> 00:24:06,510
I let you down.

349
00:24:08,270 --> 00:24:09,730
And I let your mother down.

350
00:24:12,270 --> 00:24:13,350
When I was younger,

351
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:14,830
I had a bad temper

352
00:24:16,550 --> 00:24:17,950
and heavy work pressure.

353
00:24:20,830 --> 00:24:22,690
I didn't take good care of you two.

354
00:24:26,310 --> 00:24:28,170
Later, your mother and I split up,

355
00:24:28,790 --> 00:24:31,250
making you grow up
in a single-parent family

356
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:32,720
from a young age.

357
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:34,600
I know you've carried

358
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:36,810
a lot of hurt and unhappiness inside.

359
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:38,550
I'm sorry.

360
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:42,680
None of this would have happened
otherwise.

361
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,200
Dad,

362
00:24:44,270 --> 00:24:46,930
didn't we agree
we wouldn't mention it anymore?

363
00:24:47,930 --> 00:24:48,450
Okay,

364
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,260
I won't mention it.

365
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:53,560
Then when you get better,

366
00:24:53,790 --> 00:24:55,390
I'll take you to skip stones.

367
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:56,350
I can get over a dozen skips in one throw.

368
00:24:56,350 --> 00:24:57,550
I'm really good at it.

369
00:25:00,070 --> 00:25:00,440
Okay.

370
00:25:01,350 --> 00:25:02,720
I did that too when I was little.

371
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:03,610
I was also very good at it.

372
00:25:03,610 --> 00:25:05,340
I could get over a dozen as well.

373
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:06,790
Let's have a contest.

374
00:25:06,790 --> 00:25:07,160
Sure.

375
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:26,830
[Binjiang Intermediate People's Court]

376
00:25:29,510 --> 00:25:31,510
Driver, please wait for us a moment.

377
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,510
-Long time no see.
-Long time no see.

378
00:25:33,510 --> 00:25:34,040
Gaoyuan.

379
00:25:34,830 --> 00:25:35,440
Long time no see.

380
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,160
Long time no see.

381
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,820
It really has been a long time.

382
00:25:41,490 --> 00:25:43,490
I found this while tidying up

383
00:25:43,070 --> 00:25:44,110
[Zhang Lihui]

384
00:25:43,530 --> 00:25:44,000
the room.

385
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,400
Your name is on it.

386
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:53,070
Let's go grab a meal

387
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,440
together later.

388
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:57,100
No, thanks.

389
00:25:57,610 --> 00:25:59,110
We need to hurry to the train station.

390
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:00,240
We have to head back.

391
00:26:01,110 --> 00:26:01,970
In such a hurry?

392
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,960
If I had known,
I would have mailed it to you.

393
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:04,960
That wouldn't do.

394
00:26:05,790 --> 00:26:06,550
I had to come.

395
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:09,660
Just think of this
as bringing Yingjie home.

396
00:26:13,880 --> 00:26:14,440
Let's go.

397
00:26:15,750 --> 00:26:16,550
We're leaving.

398
00:26:16,550 --> 00:26:16,880
Okay.

399
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,000
Take care.

400
00:26:19,070 --> 00:26:19,680
Take care, you two.

401
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:20,030
Okay.

402
00:26:20,510 --> 00:26:22,240
We'll leave you to it, Gaoyuan.

403
00:26:26,030 --> 00:26:26,560
Goodbye.

404
00:27:20,030 --> 00:27:22,360
I once thought
I didn't like him that much.

405
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:24,150
But that trial

406
00:27:24,550 --> 00:27:26,080
made me see his brilliance.

407
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:28,400
It was so captivating

408
00:27:28,790 --> 00:27:29,590
and so bright.

409
00:27:31,120 --> 00:27:32,720
It was a spirit that had never

410
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:33,680
been tainted.

411
00:27:34,690 --> 00:27:36,440
It was unwavering devotion and pursuit

412
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:37,700
of ideals and justice.

413
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:41,030
It was the spirit of someone
who would never

414
00:27:41,030 --> 00:27:42,030
stop being young.

415
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:46,920
Lihui.

416
00:27:47,790 --> 00:27:49,050
I have no one to talk to,

417
00:27:50,070 --> 00:27:51,600
but I'm writing to tell you.

418
00:27:52,830 --> 00:27:54,830
Maybe you'll never see this letter.

419
00:27:55,510 --> 00:27:56,270
Maybe

420
00:27:56,720 --> 00:27:58,000
when we are 80,

421
00:27:58,310 --> 00:27:59,480
we'll open it together,

422
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:00,030
read it,

423
00:28:00,590 --> 00:28:01,920
and let time

424
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:02,880
gently mock us.

425
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:06,640
Lihui.

426
00:28:07,550 --> 00:28:08,400
I love life.

427
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,310
I love my career.

428
00:28:11,350 --> 00:28:12,030
And now,

429
00:28:13,550 --> 00:28:15,880
I am also deeply in love
with Chen Yizhong.

430
00:29:15,510 --> 00:29:16,070
Comrade,

431
00:29:16,830 --> 00:29:18,030
my name is Qin Zhigao.

432
00:29:18,870 --> 00:29:20,200
I want to turn myself in.

433
00:29:23,590 --> 00:29:26,250
I am guilty
of intentional homicide by omission

434
00:29:26,550 --> 00:29:28,350
for failing to give emergency treatment

435
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:30,590
to my poisoned wife.

436
00:29:31,680 --> 00:29:33,160
She has passed away.

437
00:29:35,590 --> 00:29:36,310
I am at home.

438
00:29:58,680 --> 00:29:59,440
Mr. Chen,

439
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:02,160
what do you mean by all this?

440
00:30:03,070 --> 00:30:05,130
So you want Hu Xudong to plead guilty?

441
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:07,750
If he doesn't plead guilty
at the first‑instance trial,

442
00:30:07,750 --> 00:30:09,920
it's really bad for the trial outcome.

443
00:30:10,590 --> 00:30:11,720
I told Hu Xudong

444
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:13,200
he could retract his confession in court,

445
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,530
and that we would do our best
to defend him,

446
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:17,880
but the outcome is indeed not optimistic.

447
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:18,810
Not optimistic?

448
00:30:19,160 --> 00:30:20,890
That means he's as good as dead!

449
00:30:21,110 --> 00:30:22,570
The death penalty, right?

450
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:24,010
Dad, don't be like this.

451
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:26,060
The probability is very high.

452
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:28,350
You kept telling me to trust the law

453
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:29,880
and trust you.

454
00:30:30,920 --> 00:30:31,880
And now?

455
00:30:32,270 --> 00:30:33,350
You just throw up your hands

456
00:30:33,350 --> 00:30:35,000
and tell me it's not optimistic!

457
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:35,750
Dad, that's enough.

458
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:36,610
That's enough.

459
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:38,510
You can still appeal.

460
00:30:38,750 --> 00:30:40,350
There is still the second‑instance trial.

461
00:30:40,350 --> 00:30:40,920
Mr. Chen,

462
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:44,440
what if the first-instance trial
gives him the death penalty

463
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:46,840
and the second-instance trial upholds it?

464
00:30:49,270 --> 00:30:50,240
Actually, we are just

465
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:51,400
trying to buy more time

466
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,480
to find new evidence

467
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:53,350
and new clues.

468
00:30:54,030 --> 00:30:55,200
During the second-instance trial,
I'll try my best

469
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:55,550
and see if we can...

470
00:30:55,550 --> 00:30:56,590
Have you tried your best?

471
00:30:56,590 --> 00:30:58,550
You were the one
who said he was innocent at first!

472
00:30:58,550 --> 00:30:59,550
Now you're the one
asking him to plead guilty

473
00:30:59,550 --> 00:31:01,750
and beg for a suspended death sentence!

474
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:04,240
You really have a way with words!

475
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:06,140
Given the current situation,

476
00:31:06,310 --> 00:31:07,310
keeping him alive

477
00:31:07,830 --> 00:31:09,160
is what matters most.

478
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:12,920
Get lost!

479
00:31:13,110 --> 00:31:13,550
Dad.

480
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:24,790
Mr. Chen, I'm sorry.

481
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:27,150
I know you've done your best.

482
00:31:27,590 --> 00:31:28,680
My dad knows it too.

483
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:31,760
Let's just keep him alive first.

484
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:34,280
Otherwise, nothing else matters.

485
00:31:36,070 --> 00:31:36,510
Okay.

486
00:31:41,070 --> 00:31:42,130
I'll take my leave.

487
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,330
T-Take care, Mr. Chen.

488
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:28,880
When we were kids,

489
00:32:31,200 --> 00:32:32,660
Liu and I used to bully him.

490
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:36,610
We tied him to a tree,

491
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:40,440
hung cotton yarn on his butt,

492
00:32:42,550 --> 00:32:44,110
dipped the yarn in kerosene,

493
00:32:44,110 --> 00:32:45,110
and set it on fire.

494
00:32:47,310 --> 00:32:50,510
We called it "lighting the sky lantern."

495
00:32:53,160 --> 00:32:56,020
We got plenty of beatings
from our parents for that.

496
00:32:56,550 --> 00:32:57,550
I owe Yin Ping.

497
00:33:02,510 --> 00:33:04,440
His grandmother was a kind person.

498
00:33:06,310 --> 00:33:07,030
Every time she saw me,

499
00:33:07,030 --> 00:33:08,230
she'd give me snacks.

500
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:16,280
I'll remember her kindness
for the rest of my life.

501
00:33:18,070 --> 00:33:18,830
I owe her too.

502
00:33:26,550 --> 00:33:27,270
Let it be.

503
00:33:29,680 --> 00:33:32,010
Let them sentence me however they see fit.

504
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:36,350
If...

505
00:33:39,070 --> 00:33:40,880
If you plead guilty now,

506
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:47,640
you may get a suspended death sentence
at the first-instance trial.

507
00:33:47,640 --> 00:33:50,200
I've already retracted my confession
in court.

508
00:33:50,200 --> 00:33:51,460
Now I'm taking it back?

509
00:33:54,830 --> 00:33:55,690
There's no way.

510
00:33:56,590 --> 00:33:58,050
How is that even possible?

511
00:33:59,480 --> 00:34:00,940
I'll think of another way.

512
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:03,300
If you want to live,

513
00:34:06,270 --> 00:34:07,440
the best way now

514
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:10,510
is to aim for a suspended death sentence
in the first-instance trial.

515
00:34:10,510 --> 00:34:12,440
Plead guilty, cooperate fully,

516
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:16,449
seek the forgiveness
of the victim's family,

517
00:34:16,670 --> 00:34:17,800
and look for a chance

518
00:34:20,030 --> 00:34:21,830
to render meritorious service.

519
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:25,489
I can go to Yin Ping's uncle

520
00:34:26,030 --> 00:34:27,760
and try to get his forgiveness.

521
00:34:27,920 --> 00:34:30,120
But all of that requires compensation.

522
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:32,130
So I'll go bankrupt,

523
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:35,060
making his uncle rich?

524
00:34:37,550 --> 00:34:40,080
Then I'll rot in prison
for the rest of my life?

525
00:34:41,070 --> 00:34:42,070
I don't want that.

526
00:34:48,550 --> 00:34:49,400
Mr. Chen!

527
00:34:50,070 --> 00:34:50,600
Mr. Chen.

528
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:52,900
Don't be like this.

529
00:34:53,590 --> 00:34:55,250
I'm the one who's going to die.

530
00:34:56,030 --> 00:34:56,760
Relax.

531
00:34:58,070 --> 00:34:58,590
Smile.

532
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:00,360
Smile.

533
00:35:07,880 --> 00:35:08,760
But honestly,

534
00:35:12,630 --> 00:35:13,230
thank you.

535
00:35:14,550 --> 00:35:15,010
Really.

536
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:17,520
Thank you.

537
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:26,380
Prosecutor Zhang,

538
00:35:26,550 --> 00:35:27,440
does this mean

539
00:35:28,190 --> 00:35:29,920
Jicai will be exonerated soon?

540
00:35:30,710 --> 00:35:32,470
I can only say
the higher-ups are taking it seriously.

541
00:35:32,470 --> 00:35:35,270
They will definitely investigate it
thoroughly,

542
00:35:35,630 --> 00:35:38,190
but it still has to go
through proper procedures.

543
00:35:38,190 --> 00:35:38,780
Anyway,

544
00:35:39,090 --> 00:35:39,800
things are moving

545
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,200
in a positive direction.

546
00:35:42,150 --> 00:35:42,760
Ms. Zhang.

547
00:35:43,710 --> 00:35:44,520
Then my father

548
00:35:44,550 --> 00:35:45,760
is no longer a murderer,

549
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:46,230
right?

550
00:35:47,110 --> 00:35:49,310
Who told you your father was a murderer?

551
00:35:49,710 --> 00:35:51,030
Everyone says so.

552
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:53,090
I don't have any friends

553
00:35:53,880 --> 00:35:54,710
at school.

554
00:36:01,670 --> 00:36:04,330
I'm planning to transfer her
to another school.

555
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:06,230
These words always follow her.

556
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,960
She can't shake them off
no matter where she goes.

557
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:10,960
You are so cute.

558
00:36:11,230 --> 00:36:12,070
When you transfer to a new school,

559
00:36:12,070 --> 00:36:13,190
you will definitely have many

560
00:36:13,190 --> 00:36:13,990
good friends.

561
00:36:14,850 --> 00:36:15,400
Exactly.

562
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:17,530
Captain Lyu.

563
00:36:21,510 --> 00:36:23,170
Captain Lyu, come eat with us.

564
00:36:23,670 --> 00:36:24,480
Come in.

565
00:36:24,510 --> 00:36:25,770
What are you afraid of?

566
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:33,960
A bowl of noodles. Extra chili.

567
00:36:34,720 --> 00:36:37,040
You cried from the spiciness last time.

568
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:38,270
Do you remember that?

569
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:54,640
The chili's hot,
so I didn't put too much in it.

570
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,510
No need. It's on me.

571
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,160
Too proud to take a favor, right?

572
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:04,640
What do you mean by that?

573
00:37:04,640 --> 00:37:05,360
Why do you keep

574
00:37:05,360 --> 00:37:06,820
coming here over and over?

575
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:07,920
Looking for trouble?

576
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:08,850
Picking a fight?

577
00:37:09,710 --> 00:37:11,440
Don't you feel any guilt at all?

578
00:37:12,670 --> 00:37:13,930
How dare you come here?

579
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:15,390
How dare you eat here?

580
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:18,670
It was you.

581
00:37:20,670 --> 00:37:23,270
It was you
who wrongfully arrested my husband.

582
00:37:24,630 --> 00:37:26,630
How do you have the nerve to eat here?

583
00:37:27,550 --> 00:37:28,350
Just you wait.

584
00:37:29,070 --> 00:37:30,130
In a couple of days,

585
00:37:30,880 --> 00:37:32,280
when my husband gets out,

586
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:34,820
we'll go find you together

587
00:37:38,550 --> 00:37:40,150
and have a good talk with you.

588
00:37:44,590 --> 00:37:46,190
I'm just here to eat noodles.

589
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:49,460
Is this how you treat your customers?

590
00:37:51,550 --> 00:37:52,610
Prosecutor Zhang,

591
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:53,690
step outside for a moment.

592
00:37:53,690 --> 00:37:54,820
I need to talk to you.

593
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:07,690
Captain Lyu.

594
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:09,110
She's been holding it in
for so many years.

595
00:38:09,110 --> 00:38:10,360
She just needed an outlet.

596
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:12,020
Please don't take it to heart.

597
00:38:17,030 --> 00:38:18,880
Did the investigation team notify you?

598
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:19,540
About what?

599
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:23,210
News just came from the bureau.

600
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,940
The DNA test results are back.

601
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:27,000
What are the results?

602
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:28,230
The DNA from the skin tissue

603
00:38:28,230 --> 00:38:30,320
extracted from Lin Yan's eight fingernails

604
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:32,150
was tested
by the Ministry of Public Security,

605
00:38:32,150 --> 00:38:34,000
and it doesn't match Jia Peng's DNA.

606
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,630
In other words, the skin tissue

607
00:38:35,630 --> 00:38:36,760
is not from Jia Peng.

608
00:38:37,590 --> 00:38:38,190
Of course,

609
00:38:39,030 --> 00:38:39,760
it doesn't prove

610
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:41,320
that Jia Peng isn't the real killer.

611
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:41,800
But

612
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:44,110
it's highly possible that Jia Peng

613
00:38:44,110 --> 00:38:45,370
isn't the real killer.

614
00:38:46,150 --> 00:38:49,230
Could there be an error in the test?

615
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:52,820
Prosecutor Zhang,

616
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:55,060
your obsession is too strong.

617
00:38:55,070 --> 00:38:56,370
Haven't you always emphasized

618
00:38:56,370 --> 00:38:57,840
"the presumption of innocence"

619
00:38:57,840 --> 00:38:59,900
and "innocent until proven guilty"?

620
00:38:59,910 --> 00:39:01,440
You applied it to Yan Jicai.

621
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:03,400
You should apply it to Jia Peng too.

622
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:04,030
Shouldn't the standard

623
00:39:04,030 --> 00:39:04,840
stay the same?

624
00:39:17,150 --> 00:39:17,800
Gaoyuan.

625
00:39:20,550 --> 00:39:21,630
Has your collegial panel reached

626
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:23,290
a conclusion on that case yet?

627
00:39:23,890 --> 00:39:25,150
I've been busy
with Xia Yingjie's matter recently,

628
00:39:25,150 --> 00:39:27,150
so I haven't had time to deal with it.

629
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:37,800
When you talked to Xia,

630
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,360
did you perhaps use

631
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:40,490
the wrong approach?

632
00:39:41,360 --> 00:39:43,000
Word is spreading around the courthouse

633
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,630
that you had a fierce quarrel with Xia

634
00:39:44,630 --> 00:39:45,590
before she was attacked.

635
00:39:45,590 --> 00:39:46,320
Is that true?

636
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:51,650
We did have an argument,

637
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:54,280
because of those photos.

638
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:57,810
Xia Yingjie didn't believe

639
00:39:57,840 --> 00:39:59,030
that because of this,

640
00:39:59,030 --> 00:40:01,030
the court questioned her judgment.

641
00:40:08,150 --> 00:40:09,110
As your superior,

642
00:40:09,110 --> 00:40:09,590
I really

643
00:40:09,590 --> 00:40:11,250
have to criticize you on this.

644
00:40:12,670 --> 00:40:14,070
As the deputy court president,

645
00:40:14,070 --> 00:40:16,110
you failed to consider the bigger picture

646
00:40:16,110 --> 00:40:17,840
and kept delaying the verdict.

647
00:40:18,190 --> 00:40:19,520
As the presiding judge,

648
00:40:19,540 --> 00:40:20,330
you failed

649
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:21,900
to recuse yourself from improper contact
with the defendant's lawyer,

650
00:40:21,900 --> 00:40:22,670
leaving behind those ambiguous photos

651
00:40:22,670 --> 00:40:23,630
open to misinterpretation.

652
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:24,690
As the supervisor,

653
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,000
when your subordinate got emotional,

654
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:27,730
you failed to handle it in time!

655
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:29,480
So you bear responsibility

656
00:40:29,480 --> 00:40:30,550
for what happened to Xia!

657
00:40:30,550 --> 00:40:31,320
Do you understand?

658
00:40:31,320 --> 00:40:32,720
You should know very well

659
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:35,960
that those photos

660
00:40:36,190 --> 00:40:38,120
were taken with ulterior motives.

661
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:43,190
That restaurant sits
right below our courthouse.

662
00:40:43,190 --> 00:40:44,280
In the past, after court sessions,

663
00:40:44,280 --> 00:40:45,900
prosecutors, judges, and lawyers...

664
00:40:45,900 --> 00:40:47,150
All our colleagues ate there.

665
00:40:47,150 --> 00:40:47,730
Running into each other

666
00:40:47,730 --> 00:40:49,460
is perfectly normal, isn't it?

667
00:40:50,810 --> 00:40:52,070
If I had wanted to meet privately,

668
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:53,250
couldn't I have chosen

669
00:40:53,250 --> 00:40:53,590
a more secluded place?

670
00:40:53,590 --> 00:40:55,720
Couldn't I have booked a private room?

671
00:40:56,800 --> 00:40:58,320
Although we were classmates,

672
00:40:58,320 --> 00:40:59,250
Court Pres. Qiu,

673
00:40:59,850 --> 00:41:01,360
as long as you've read the trial records,

674
00:41:01,360 --> 00:41:01,780
you'll know

675
00:41:01,780 --> 00:41:02,630
that neither Xia Yingjie nor I

676
00:41:02,630 --> 00:41:03,630
said a single word

677
00:41:03,630 --> 00:41:04,960
in favor of the defense!

678
00:41:08,230 --> 00:41:09,560
As the court president,

679
00:41:10,510 --> 00:41:11,360
if you had

680
00:41:11,360 --> 00:41:12,300
smoothed things over,

681
00:41:12,300 --> 00:41:12,960
maybe...

682
00:41:14,070 --> 00:41:14,800
How come it was on me

683
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:16,060
to smooth things over?

684
00:41:16,670 --> 00:41:17,110
Yu Gaoyuan,

685
00:41:17,110 --> 00:41:18,510
explain yourself clearly!

686
00:41:18,510 --> 00:41:20,030
What does this have to do with me?

687
00:41:20,030 --> 00:41:22,160
Did I say it had anything to do with you?

688
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:24,600
It has nothing to do with you.

689
00:41:24,710 --> 00:41:25,570
Nothing at all.

690
00:41:26,110 --> 00:41:26,820
I just wanted to say

691
00:41:26,820 --> 00:41:28,220
that you should trust us.

692
00:41:33,190 --> 00:41:33,720
Besides,

693
00:41:34,190 --> 00:41:35,280
we act according to the law,

694
00:41:35,280 --> 00:41:37,040
letting the chips fall where they may.

695
00:41:37,040 --> 00:41:37,900
If we can't even

696
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,030
maintain the most basic composure
in the face

697
00:41:39,030 --> 00:41:39,550
of gossip and rumors,

698
00:41:39,550 --> 00:41:40,460
how can we be judges?

699
00:41:40,460 --> 00:41:41,650
How can we make the public trust us

700
00:41:41,650 --> 00:41:42,650
and trust the law?

701
00:41:51,150 --> 00:41:52,350
Are you lecturing me?

702
00:42:02,400 --> 00:42:03,630
What are you going to do

703
00:42:03,630 --> 00:42:04,590
with the Hu Xudong case?

704
00:42:04,590 --> 00:42:05,790
I plan to be cautious.

705
00:42:15,880 --> 00:42:18,610
It goes
to the Adjudication Committee tomorrow!

706
00:42:32,070 --> 00:42:32,670
Given the two

707
00:42:32,670 --> 00:42:34,400
key pieces of evidence we have,

708
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:36,160
namely the murder weapon

709
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:37,420
and the bloodstained clothing,

710
00:42:37,420 --> 00:42:39,280
we cannot conclusively identify

711
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:40,770
the defendant as the real killer.

712
00:42:40,770 --> 00:42:42,230
The rest of the evidence is also…

713
00:42:42,230 --> 00:42:42,710
Yu,

714
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:44,840
your collegial panel's proposal
for a suspended death sentence

715
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:46,240
is self-contradictory.

716
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:48,760
The defendant retracted his confession
in court,

717
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:49,630
had a bad attitude,

718
00:42:49,630 --> 00:42:51,280
and refused to pay compensation.

719
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:52,330
There's not

720
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:53,960
a single mitigating factor.

721
00:42:54,150 --> 00:42:55,510
And you propose
a suspended death sentence?

722
00:42:55,510 --> 00:42:57,110
Doesn't this obviously show

723
00:42:57,150 --> 00:42:59,150
that we lack confidence in the case?

724
00:42:59,670 --> 00:43:00,730
In the old days,

725
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:02,320
this would have been
a clear death penalty case.
